INSERT INTO public.generic_medicines (generic_name, description, atc_code)
VALUES ('Bevacizumab', 'Used as part of combination therapy for metastatic colorectal cancer and HER2-negative metastatic breast cancer. In August 2014 the US FDA granted additional approval for metastatic cervical cancer. In November 2014, FDA approval was extended to include a combination therapy of bevacizumab plus chemotherapy (, pegylated liposomal or ) for platinum-resistant, recurrent ovarian cancer (based on findings from the Phase 3 AURELIA clinical trial ). Additional Phase 2 clinical trial results are provided in . In June 2018, FDA approval was further expanded to include the treatment of epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube, or primary peritoneal cancer in combination with and paclitaxel, followed by single-agent bevacizumab, in patients with stage III or IV disease, and to be used after initial surgical resection . Clinical trials evaluating bevacizumab in combination with the immune checkpoint inhibitors (anti-CTLA4) or (anti-PD-1) in advanced solid malignancies are underway (for example - Phase 2 stage III-IV melanoma; - Phase 1 stage IIIB/IV non-small cell lung cancer). A re-engineered version of bevacizumab with a different glycosylation profile (bevacizumab beta, ABP 215) is in Phase 3 clinical trial for metastatic non-small cell lung cancers (NSCLC), This trial, is comparing bevacizumab beta vs. the original , Bevacizumab (Avastin®) is sometimes prescribed ''off-label'' as a therapy for wet age-related macular degeneration (AMD), as an alternative to (Lucentis®) and (Eylea®). SARS-CoV-2 and COVID-19: Bevacizumab has been entered into clinical trials in patients with COVID-19, to determine if suppression of vascular permeability will reduce pulmonary edema in severe/critical COVID-19 patients.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (generic_name) DO UPDATE SET description = EXCLUDED.description;

