INSERT INTO public.generic_medicines (generic_name, description, atc_code)
VALUES ('Ramucirumab', 'In 2012, the EMA granted orphan drug approval for ramucirumab for the treatment of hepatocellular carcinoma and gastric cancer. The US FDA granted full approval in 2014 firstly as a monotherapy for the treatment of advanced stomach cancer or adenocarcinoma of the gastroesophageal junction, and latterly in combination with for the same patient group. Ramucirumab was approved by the FDA to treat patients with metastatic non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) in December 2014. Further approval was granted in April 2015 for the treatment of patients with metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC) in combination with FOLFIRI (, , and ) chemotherapy and in particular for patients with disease progression on or after prior therapy with , , and a fluoropyrimidine (eg , , or ). In May 2019, the FDA expanded approval to include the treatment of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) patients who are intolerant of, or who have experienced disease progression on or after treatment with the kinase inhibitor , and who have an elevated baseline alpha fetoprotein (≥400 ng/mL). This approval was based on results from clinical trial which showed that in these patients ramucirumab increased overall survival by 1.2 months compared to placebo . Click to link to ClinicalTrials.gov''s full list of ramucirumab trials. June 2020 saw FDA approval expanded to include use of ramucirumab in combination with the small molecule EGFR inhibitor , as first-line treatment for metastatic NSCLC with epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) exon 19 deletions or exon 21 (L858R) mutations.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (generic_name) DO UPDATE SET description = EXCLUDED.description;

