VALUES ('Edoxaban', 'This drug was initially approved in Japan for the treatment of venous thromboembolism (VTE). Subsequently, in 2015, the US FDA and EMA approved edoxaban to reduce the risk of stroke and systemic embolism in patients with atrial fibrillation that is not caused by a heart valve problem and to treat deep vein thrombosis (DVT) and pulmonary embolism (PE) in patients who have already received anti-clotting therapy for five to ten days.', NULL)
