INSERT INTO public.generic_medicines (generic_name, description, atc_code)
VALUES ('Risankizumab', 'Results from the first-in-human proof-of-concept trial in patients with psoriasis were reported by Krueger et al. in 2015 . Phase 3 trial results in psoriasis patients were published in 2018 . FDA and EMA approvals were granted in 2019 and it is also approved in Japan and Canada. Risankizumab therapy is indicated for patients with moderate to severe plaque psoriasis who are candidates for systemic therapy or phototherapy (Japan''s authorisation additionally includes treatment of generalized pustular psoriasis, erythrodermic psoriasis and psoriatic arthritis). Investigations are ongoing in other autoinflammatory conditions. Click to link to ClinicalTrials.gov''s full list of risankizumab trials. In May 2022, two studies reported results from phase 3 RCTs of risankizumab for Crohn''s disease . The NCT04524611 (SEQUENCE) study is directly comparing risankizumab and ustekinumab in participants with moderate to severe Crohn''s disease and for whom anti-TNF therapy has failed.', NULL)
