INSERT INTO public.generic_medicines (generic_name, description, atc_code)
VALUES ('Abrocitinib', 'Abrocitinib (PF-04965842) was advanced to clinical trials for autoimmune conditions, and reached Phase 3 evaluation for atopic dermatitis and Phase 2 for plaque psoriasis (). Results from the psoriasis trial have been published , and these indicated that PF-04965842 improved disease symptoms and was well tolerated in patients with moderate to severe psoriasis. Further development for psoriasis has been terminated by the sponsor (Pfizer) for business reasons. Development in moderate to severe atopic dermatitis is continuing in Pfizer''s JAK1 Atopic Dermatitis Efficacy and Safety (JADE) program, which incluides the JADE MONO-1 () and JADE MONO-2 () trials. Results demonstrating significant efficacy in the JADE MONO-1 study were published in July 2020 , and similarly supportive results from JADE MONO-2 followed in August 2020 . Abrocitinib was first approved for clinical use in 2021. Under these authorisations it is indicated as a treatment for moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis in adult patients who are candidates for systemic therapy. The FDA''s approval as a treatment for atopic dermatitis was granted in January 2022. Abrocitinib has been used off-label to demonstrate proof-of-concept for JAK inhibitor therapy as a curative intervention for toxic epidermal necrolysis (TEN) .', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (generic_name) DO UPDATE SET description = EXCLUDED.description;

